inline constexpr std::array<FxLine, 176> kLines{{
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.about-blackwood", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.about-blackwood", "This is the Blackwood Road. About 640 yards east of the station is Cartwright's Cross, where the signpost arms point east to Gideon and back west to Leyawiin. West of the station the road runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh, then on through the Blackwood hills to Leyawiin in Cyrodiil. We are the road's water point at the ford. The roads are flooded in the monsoon.", "This is the Blackwood Road. East of us, about 640 yards, is Cartwright's Cross, where the arms point east to Gideon and back west to Leyawiin. West, about 450 yards, is the edge of Black Marsh. The road goes on to Leyawiin.", "This is the Blackwood Road. About 640 yards east of the station is Cartwright's Cross, where the signpost arms point east to Gideon and back west to Leyawiin. West of the station the road runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh, then on through the Blackwood hills to Leyawiin in Cyrodiil. We are the road's water point at the ford. Travellers stop for it. The roads are flooded in the monsoon. When the road is open, we live by the trade with Leyawiin.", -1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.about-claywater", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.about-claywater", "Claywater is a mixed village where the road crosses the ford. An Imperial well and station house stand on this bank. An Argonian landing stands on the other. Neither side can hold the other's bank, so they share the ford. A traveller can rest safely here and have shelter for the night.", "A mixed village where the road crosses the Claywater ford. The station is on this bank and the landing on the other.", "Claywater is a mixed village where the road crosses the ford. An Imperial well and station house stand on this bank. An Argonian landing stands on the other. Neither side can hold the other's bank, so they share the ford. A traveller can rest safely here and have shelter for the night.", -1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.about-gideon", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.about-gideon", "Gideon is the western frontier city at the east end of the Blackwood Road, where the courts still work. From the station it is about 640 yards to the signpost at Cartwright's Cross. From the signpost it is about 1,190 yards more, a little over a mile in all. Its courthouse is the last that works in these parts. Disputes are still settled there on written record.", "Gideon is the city at the east end of this road, a little over a mile on.", "Gideon is the western frontier city at the east end of the Blackwood Road, where the courts still work. From the station it is about 640 yards to the signpost at Cartwright's Cross. From the signpost it is about 1,190 yards more, a little over a mile in all. Its courthouse is the last that works in these parts. Disputes are still settled there on written record.", -1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.about-imperial", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.about-imperial", "The Empire left the well and the station house. I serve an office, but the Empire has sent no pay for generations. I keep faith with the well.", "The Empire left us the well and the station house. No pay has come from Cyrodiil in generations.", "The Empire left the well and the station house. I am glad of both. No pay has come from Cyrodiil in generations. I keep faith with the well.", -1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.about-imperial-legion-remnant", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.about-imperial-legion-remnant", "The Legion is the Empire here. The garrisons left behind still keep the rolls and drill. Their heirs keep the old ranks without pay. I keep faith with the well.", "The Legion is the Empire here. Some keep the old ranks and drill without pay.", "The Legion is the Empire here. The garrisons left behind still keep the rolls and drill. Their heirs keep the old ranks without pay. I keep faith with the well and with no man in Cyrodiil. I will say so to any traveller.", -1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.about-onkobra", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.about-onkobra", "The Onkobra is the river that runs east through Gideon into the interior. The stream at our ford is not the Onkobra. It runs west, away from Gideon. I know the ford and where it can be waded. Ask at the landing about the water beyond it. The landing's people work it.", "The Onkobra runs through Gideon. The stream at our ford is not the Onkobra.", "The Onkobra is the river that runs east through Gideon into the interior. The stream at our ford is not the Onkobra. It runs west, away from Gideon. I know the ford and where it can be waded. Ask at the landing about the water beyond it. The landing's people work it. They are good neighbours.", -1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.about-prison-road", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.about-prison-road", "This is not the Prison road. The Prison road is the old Imperial cordon road from Blackrose to Lilmoth, far to the south-east. The road through Claywater Station is the Blackwood Road. At Cartwright's Cross the signpost arms point east to Gideon and back west to Leyawiin.", "This is not the Prison road. That one is far to the south-east. Ours is the Blackwood Road.", "This is not the Prison road, citizen. The Prison road is the old Imperial cordon road from Blackrose to Lilmoth, far to the south-east. The road through Claywater Station is the Blackwood Road. At Cartwright's Cross the signpost arms point east to Gideon and back west to Leyawiin. I keep the well. I know no more of the south-east.", -1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.claywater-station", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-station", "Two halves at one ford. Neither can hold the other's bank. My side is stone and old timber. The landing is mud and thatch.", "Two halves at one ford. Neither can hold the other's bank.", "Two halves at one ford. Neither can hold the other's bank. The station is built of Imperial timber framing and well masonry. The landing has Argonian mud walls and thatch. The two halves face each other over the water.", -1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.claywater-station-danger.crocodile", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-station-danger", "A crocodile lies in the deep pool under the clay cut below the ford, where the landing digs its plaster clay. It suns on the bank at midday. It comes up at any traveller on it, day or night. Keep away from it after dark.", "A crocodile lies in the deep pool under the clay cut. It comes up at any traveller on it. Keep away.", "A crocodile lies in the deep pool under the clay cut below the ford, where the landing digs its plaster clay. It suns on the bank at midday. It comes up at any traveller on it, day or night. If you must go there, go by day. The station's low wall above the cut gives a safer view. I suspect some travellers wade the shallow tail of the river below it at night to dodge the landing's charge.", 0, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.claywater-station-danger.general", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-station-danger", "I keep watch on the well at night. Do not wade the river after dark. I do not hold with wading to dodge a charge.", "I keep watch on the well at night. Do not wade the river after dark.", "I keep watch on the well at night. Do not wade the river after dark. I do not hold with wading to dodge a charge. I suspect some travellers wade the shallow tail of the river below the clay cut at night for that reason.", 1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.claywater-station-directions.cut", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-station-directions", "To the road, go east about 640 yards to Cartwright's Cross. The raft and the landing stage are about 65 yards north of the well, across the ford. The clay cut is below the ford on this bank: from the well, go about 45 yards west, outside the low stone walls, to where the river swings west under a bare clay bank and the water lies deep and dark. If the bank flattens into reeds, you have gone past it.", "East along the road to Cartwright's Cross, about 640 yards. The clay cut is 45 yards west of the well, outside the low walls. The raft is 65 yards north.", "To the road, go east about 640 yards to Cartwright's Cross, where the arms point to Gideon and to Leyawiin. The raft and the landing stage are about 65 yards north of the well, across the ford. The clay cut is below the ford on this bank: from the well, go about 45 yards west, outside the low stone walls, to where the river swings west under a bare clay bank and the water lies deep and dark. If the bank flattens into reeds, you have gone past it. I am at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk.", 2, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.claywater-station-directions.general", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-station-directions", "Go east along the road about 640 yards to Cartwright's Cross, where the arms point east to Gideon and back west to Leyawiin. Gideon lies about 1,190 yards beyond the signpost, a little over a mile from here. Leyawiin lies west. The road runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh and on from there. On the way east you will pass the Drowning Gate, a painted pole barrier in a field about 110 yards off the road on your left. The raft and the landing stage are about 65 yards north of the well, across the ford. The round mud huts stand behind them on the far bank.", "East along the road, about 640 yards, to Cartwright's Cross. Gideon is about 1,190 yards beyond it. West is Leyawiin. The raft is 65 yards north of the well, across the ford.", "Go east along the road about 640 yards to Cartwright's Cross, where the arms point east to Gideon and back west to Leyawiin. Gideon lies about 1,190 yards beyond the signpost, a little over a mile from here. Leyawiin lies west. The road runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh and on from there. On the way east you will pass the Drowning Gate, a painted pole barrier in a field about 110 yards off the road on your left. The raft and the landing stage are about 65 yards north of the well, across the ford. The round mud huts stand behind them on the far bank. I am at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk, if you need me.", 3, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.claywater-station-people", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-station-people", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is the landing's poler. He poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon. Gaius Vibius, Keeps-The-Second-Ledger and Takes-The-Short-Weight keep the household hut by the common on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning they cook at the common's fire. By day they work the common and the drying racks. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh are travellers on the road. In the afternoon they sit on the bench by the brazier at the well. At night they pay for a bed in the station house. Quarrels go to me on this bank and to the poler on the other.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is the landing's poler. Gaius Vibius, Keeps-The-Second-Ledger and Takes-The-Short-Weight keep the household hut on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. I deal in water. I will say no more than that.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is the landing's poler. He poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon. Gaius Vibius, Keeps-The-Second-Ledger and Takes-The-Short-Weight keep the household hut by the common on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning they cook at the common's fire. By day they work the common and the drying racks. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh are travellers on the road. In the afternoon they sit on the bench by the brazier at the well. At night they pay for a bed in the station house. Quarrels go to me on this bank and to the poler on the other.", -1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.claywater-station-work", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-station-work", "We have water, beds and a stable on this bank. The cart raft crosses from the other. Each bank charges a traveller for its own half of the stop. The well is drawn at set hours by the windlass. Ask me before you draw.", "Water, beds and a stable on this bank. The cart raft is on the other.", "We have water, beds and a stable on this bank. The cart raft crosses from the other. Each bank charges a traveller for its own half of the stop, so the well and the landing charge separately for the same stop. The well is drawn at set hours by the windlass. Ask me before you draw. You are welcome to rest within the walls.", -1, 0, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.cracked-well.admit", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-cracked-well", "You have found the yearly mending, then. Very well. The lining has cracked every year. Each dry season I have re-mortared it myself. It has not held. A mason's proper lining in stone will hold where my mortar did not. Say what you mean to do about the station's charge.", "Very well. It has cracked every year. I have mended it myself each dry season. It would not hold. A mason's lining would. Say what you mean to do about the station's charge.", "You have found the yearly mending, then. I will not deny it. The lining has cracked every year. Each dry season I have re-mortared it myself. It has not held. I am tired of mending it. A mason's proper lining in stone will hold where my mortar did not. Say what you mean to do about the station's charge.", 4, 0, 1, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.cracked-well.after-40", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-cracked-well", "A band of fresh grey clay is rammed in behind the coping and down the lining on the ford side. I send for no mason. I will watch how it fares through the rains.", "Clay is rammed in on the ford side. I send for no mason.", "A band of fresh grey clay is rammed in behind the coping and down the lining on the ford side. I did not think to see clay in an Imperial well, but it is the landing's work and I agreed to it. I send for no mason. I will watch how it fares through the rains.", 5, 1, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.cracked-well.after-other", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-cracked-well", "The crack stands, a finger wide from the coping down the lining on the ford side. I enter it in the ledger each morning.", "It is cracked still. A finger wide on the ford side.", "The crack stands, a finger wide from the coping down the lining on the ford side. I enter it in the ledger each morning. I do not like to see it, citizen.", 6, 1, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.cracked-well.argue", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-cracked-well", "The new crack runs a finger wide from the coping down the lining on the ford side. It lets the ford in. Only a mason's proper lining in stone will hold. How the lining has fared in other years I will not discuss with a stranger.", "The crack lets the ford in. A mason's lining will mend it. I will say no more of the lining's past.", "The new crack runs a finger wide from the coping down the lining on the ford side. It lets the ford in. That is why I want a mason. A proper lining in stone must go in before the rains. It will hold. How the lining has fared in other years I keep to myself until I know you better.", 7, 1, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.goodbye", "goodbye", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "", "Good day, citizen. Gods keep the road dry.", "Good day.", "Good day to you, citizen. Gods keep the road dry. Come back when you need water.", -1, 1, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.greeting.active", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "", "Citizen. The well is drawn at set hours. State your business.", "You again. State your business, citizen.", "Citizen, welcome back. I am glad to see you well. What may I do for you?", 8, 1, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.greeting.after-40", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "", "Good day, citizen. The stop is one charge now: two drakes, one to each bank. The landing's clay is rammed in behind the lining.", "The station is open. One charge, two drakes the stop. Be quick, citizen.", "A pleasant day to you, citizen. I am glad to see you well. Look at the ford side of the lining. The clay is rammed in fresh behind the coping. The stop is one charge of two drakes, one to each bank.", 9, 1, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.greeting.after-41", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "", "Good day, citizen. The stop is two drakes, as before. The lining is cracked still. I hold that only a mason's lining will mend it.", "Two drakes the stop. The lining is cracked still. Pay or pass, citizen.", "A pleasant day to you, citizen. I am glad to see you well. The stop is two drakes, as before. The crack stands. A mason is still wanted.", 10, 1, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.greeting.after-42", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "", "Good day, citizen. The stop is one drake, as it was before this season. I have put it back.", "One drake the stop, as of old. Pay it, citizen.", "A pleasant day to you, citizen. I am glad to see you well. The stop is one drake again, as it was before this season.", 11, 1, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.greeting.after-90", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "", "Good day, citizen. The rains have come. The stop is two drakes still. The lining is cracked still.", "The rains are here. Two drakes the stop. The lining is cracked. Pay or pass, citizen.", "A pleasant day to you, citizen, though a wet one. The rains have come. The stop is two drakes still. The lining is cracked still.", 12, 1, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.greeting.after-93", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "", "Good day, citizen. There is no poler at the raft now. The people of the landing are in mourning. They will make no terms with the station. The stop is two drakes.", "No poler at the raft. Two drakes the stop. Pay or pass, citizen.", "A pleasant day to you, citizen. I am sorry for the landing's loss. There is no poler at the raft now. The people of the landing will make no terms with the station while they mourn. The stop is two drakes still.", 13, 1, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.greeting.start", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "", "Good day, citizen. The station is open. The stop is two drakes this season. If you want to know why there are two charges at Claywater, ask me.", "The station is open. Two drakes the stop. Pay or pass, citizen.", "A pleasant day to you, citizen. I am glad to see you well. The station is open. The well is drawn at set hours. The stop is two drakes this season. Ask me about the two charges at Claywater. I will tell you plainly.", 14, 1, 1, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.greeting.start-off-season", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "", "Good day, citizen. The station is open. We have water, beds and a stable on this bank.", "The station is open. What do you want?", "A pleasant day to you, citizen. What may I do for you?", 15, 2, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.landing-terms.20", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-landing-terms", "A mason's stone will mend the well. The landing refused to haul stone for a new lining. It does not build in stone and does not drink the well's water. Yet it would take half a charge for water that it never draws. Its people draw only to wash. I charge them nothing. If you would hear the landing's side of it, Takes-The-Short-Weight lives in the round mud hut on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning she sits at the landing's fire, about 50 yards north of the raft.", "A mason's stone will mend the well. The landing would take half a charge for water that it never draws. Its people draw only to wash. I charge them nothing.", "A mason's stone will mend the well. I will say it as often as you ask. The landing refused to haul stone for a new lining. It does not build in stone and does not drink the well's water. Yet it would take half a charge for water that it never draws. Its people draw only to wash. I charge them nothing. If you would hear the landing's side of it, Takes-The-Short-Weight lives in the round mud hut on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning she sits at the landing's fire, about 50 yards north of the raft. I am at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk.", 16, 2, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.landing-terms.30", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-landing-terms", "My objection stands. A mason's stone will mend the well. The landing would take half a charge for water that it never draws. Its people draw only to wash. I charge them nothing. If you would take it to the landing, Signs-For-The-Cargo, the landing's poler, poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon. I am at the well in the morning and at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon.", "My objection stands. A mason's stone will mend the well. The landing would take half a charge for water that it never draws. I charge its people nothing.", "My objection stands, though I will hear an answer to it. A mason's stone will mend the well. The landing would take half a charge for water that it never draws. Its people draw only to wash. I charge them nothing. If you would take it to the landing, Signs-For-The-Cargo, the landing's poler, poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon. I am at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk.", 17, 2, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.landing-terms.after-40", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-landing-terms", "The terms are made. The stop is two drakes, one to each bank. The landing's drake buys its clay behind the lining. I charge the landing's people nothing for water. I will keep to that.", "The terms are made. The landing has one drake of the two. I charge its people nothing for water.", "The terms are made. I am glad of it. The stop is two drakes, one to each bank. The landing's drake buys its clay behind the lining. I charge the landing's people nothing for water. I will keep to that. They are good neighbours.", 18, 2, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.landing-terms.after-other", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-landing-terms", "No terms were made with the landing for the well. I have not changed in this: I charge its people nothing for water.", "No terms were made with the landing for the well. I charge its people nothing for water.", "No terms were made with the landing for the well. I have not changed in this: I charge its people nothing for water. I will keep to that. It is entered in the ledger as it stands.", 19, 2, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.one-charge.after-40", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "It is done. The stop costs two drakes, one to each bank. The landing's drake buys its clay behind the lining. The landing renews the clay each dry season.", "It is done. The stop costs two drakes, one to each bank.", "It is done. The stop costs two drakes, one to each bank. The landing's drake buys its clay behind the lining. The landing renews the clay each dry season. I thank you for the trouble. I will see that it does so when the dry season comes.", 20, 2, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.one-charge.after-other", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "The one charge was never agreed at Claywater. I take my charge at the well. The landing takes its own at the ford. That is how it stands.", "The one charge was never agreed. I take mine at the well. The landing takes its own.", "The one charge was never agreed at Claywater. I take my charge at the well. The landing takes its own at the ford. That is how it stands. It is entered in the ledger so.", 21, 2, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.one-charge.agree", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "Two drakes a stop, one to each bank. The landing's drake pays for its clay behind the lining, renewed each dry season. Agreed. Let the landing ram its clay in behind the lining.", "Two drakes a stop, one to each bank. Agreed. Ram the clay in.", "Two drakes a stop, one to each bank. The landing's drake pays for its clay behind the lining, renewed each dry season. I agree. I thank you for the trouble. I charge the landing's people nothing for water. I will keep to that. Let the landing ram its clay in behind the lining before the rains.", 22, 2, 0, 0},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.one-charge.argued", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "You say clay behind the lining bends with the bank. Mortar cracks. I have mended that lining each dry season. Each season it has cracked again. I look at the new crack, a finger wide down the ford side. I cannot answer you. I give up the stone. The other objection stands, if the landing has not yet promised its clay. It would take half a charge for water it never draws. It must show me what it gives for it.", "Clay bends with the bank where mortar cracks. I have seen my mortar fail. I cannot answer that. Very well, I give up the stone. The other objection stands, if the landing has not promised its clay. It must show me what it gives.", "You argue it well, citizen. You say clay behind the lining bends with the bank. Mortar cracks. I have mended that lining myself each dry season. Each season it has cracked again. I look at the new crack, a finger wide down the ford side. I cannot answer you. I give up the stone. I thank you for the plain speaking. The other objection stands, if the landing has not yet promised its clay. It would take half a charge for water it never draws. I charge its people nothing. It must show me what it gives for it.", 23, 2, 0, 1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.one-charge.open-half", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "I cannot agree to it yet. The landing would take half a charge for water that it never draws. Its people draw only to wash. I charge them nothing. Show me what the landing will give for it. Then I will hear the rest.", "No. The landing would take half a charge for water that it never draws. Show me what it will give for it.", "I would like to agree, but I cannot yet. The landing would take half a charge for water that it never draws. Its people draw only to wash. I charge them nothing. Show me the landing will give something for it. Then I will hear the rest.", 24, 2, 1, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.one-charge.open-stone", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "I cannot agree to it yet. A mason's stone will mend the well. Mud has no place in an Imperial well. Show me the lining has failed before. Then I will hear the rest.", "No. A mason's stone will mend the well. Mud has no place in an Imperial well. Show me the lining has failed before.", "I would like to agree, but I cannot yet. A mason's stone will mend the well. Mud has no place in an Imperial well. Show me that I am wrong about the lining. Then I will hear the rest.", 25, 3, 1, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.role-well.clayed", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.role-well", "The well is Imperial-built. It is the road's water point at the ford. It is drawn at set hours by the windlass. Ask me before you draw. A band of fresh grey clay is rammed in behind the coping and down the lining on the ford side.", "The well is Imperial-built. Ask me before you draw. The clay is rammed in on the ford side.", "The well is Imperial-built. It is the road's water point at the ford. It is drawn at set hours by the windlass. Ask me before you draw. A band of fresh grey clay is rammed in behind the coping and down the lining on the ford side. Do not call the water sour in my hearing.", 26, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.role-well.general", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.role-well", "The well is Imperial-built. It is the road's water point at the ford. The windlass is worked at set hours. It is worked only with my leave. Do not call the water sour in my hearing.", "The well is Imperial-built. Ask me before you draw.", "The well is Imperial-built. It is the road's water point at the ford. The windlass is worked at set hours. It is worked only with my leave. It has a new crack a finger wide on the ford side. It needs a mason. Do not call the water sour in my hearing, citizen. When the road is open, we live by the trade with Leyawiin. The well is why travellers stop.", 27, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.stop-charge.after-42", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-stop-charge", "I dropped my charge to the old drake. It stands there. I will not say why. I ask you not to press me.", "I dropped my charge to the old drake. That is all I will say.", "I dropped my charge to the old drake. It stands there. I will not say why, even to you, citizen. I would take it kindly if you did not ask again.", 28, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.stop-charge.after-other", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-stop-charge", "I did not drop my charge to the old drake, and I do not mean to. The stop is two drakes.", "I have not dropped it. The stop is two drakes.", "I did not drop my charge to the old drake. I do not mean to, citizen. The stop is two drakes. It is entered in the ledger so.", 29, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.stop-charge.defend", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-stop-charge", "The charge stands. Two drakes a stop is what a mason costs. The well must be re-lined in stone. I will not drop it on your word.", "The charge stands. Two drakes. It pays the mason. Do not argue it.", "The charge stands. I do not set it lightly. Two drakes a stop is what a mason costs. The well must be re-lined in stone. I will not drop it on your word alone.", 30, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.stop-charge.drop", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-stop-charge", "Enough. I will drop the rise. The stop goes back to the old drake. I do not want it known how the lining has fared.", "Enough. I will drop the rise. The stop goes back to one drake.", "You have worn me down. You were right to. I will drop the rise. The stop goes back to the old drake. I do not want it known that the lining has cracked every year. I have mended it myself each dry season.", 31, 4, 0, 2},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.stop-charge.hold", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.lf83-stop-charge", "I know what you found. I will not speak of it, or drop the charge, for a stranger whom I do not yet trust.", "I know what you found. I will not drop the charge for you. Not yet.", "I know what you found. I know why you ask. But I will not drop the charge until I trust you more.", 32, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.two-charges.after-40", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "That was before the rains. The stop costs two drakes, one to each bank. The landing's clay is rammed in behind the lining. The lining is not being rebuilt. The ferry at the Drowning Gate carries you free, I am told.", "One charge now. The stop costs two drakes. The clay is in. I send for no mason.", "That was before the rains, citizen. The stop costs two drakes, one to each bank. The landing's clay is rammed in behind the lining. The lining is not being rebuilt. I did not think mud would be let into an Imperial well. I will watch how it fares. I thank you for the trouble you took. The ferry at the Drowning Gate carries you free, I am told.", 33, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.two-charges.after-41", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "That was before the rains. The stop costs two drakes, paid once at the well. The landing takes nothing from walkers this season. I am told that was your doing. The lining is cracked still. I still hold that only a mason's stone will mend it.", "Two drakes at the well, paid once. The walkers wade free. The lining is cracked still.", "That was before the rains, citizen. The stop costs two drakes, paid once at the well. The landing takes nothing from walkers this season. I am told you paid the poler a hundred drakes for it. That was handsomely done. The lining is cracked still. I still hold that only a mason's stone will mend it.", 34, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.two-charges.after-42", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "That was before the rains. The stop costs one drake, as of old. The landing has dropped its walkers' charge in answer. The lining is cracked still. Why I dropped it is my own affair. I will not discuss it. The ferry at the Drowning Gate carries you free, I am told.", "The stop costs one drake, as of old. The walkers wade free. It is settled.", "That was before the rains, citizen. The stop costs one drake, as of old. The landing has dropped its walkers' charge in answer. The lining is cracked still. Why I dropped it is my own affair. I do not discuss it, even with you. The ferry at the Drowning Gate carries you free, I am told.", 35, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.two-charges.after-90", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "The rains have come. No terms were made. Both charges stand. The stop costs two drakes at the well. Walkers pay one drake a head at the ford. The lining is cracked still.", "The rains are here. Both charges stand. The lining is cracked still.", "The rains have come, citizen. No terms were made. Both charges stand. The stop costs two drakes at the well. Walkers pay one drake a head at the ford. The lining is cracked still. I would have had it settled before the rains. I am sorry it was not.", 36, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.two-charges.after-93", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is dead. The raft is tied up at the landing stage. He died before terms were made. Both charges stand.", "The poler is dead. The raft is tied up. Both charges stand.", "I am sorry for the landing's loss, citizen. Signs-For-The-Cargo died before terms were made. The raft is tied up at the landing stage. Both charges stand.", 37, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.two-charges.cut", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "My charge has not changed. Two drakes a stop pays the mason. A proper lining in stone will hold. If you mean to go to the landing's clay cut, go about 45 yards west of the well, outside the low stone walls, to where the river swings west under a bare clay bank and the water lies deep and dark. If the bank flattens into reeds, you have gone past it. A crocodile lies in the pool below. It suns on the bank at midday. It comes up at any traveller on it, day or night. The station's low wall stands above the cut. I suspect the landing's clay basket lies there, but I cannot swear to it.", "My charge stands: two drakes, for the mason. The clay cut is about 45 yards west of the well, outside the low walls, under a bare clay bank over deep dark water. A crocodile lies in the pool and comes up at any traveller on it. If the bank flattens into reeds, you have gone past it.", "My charge has not changed. I hope you will hear me out. Two drakes a stop pays the mason. A proper lining in stone will hold. If you mean to go to the landing's clay cut, go about 45 yards west of the well, outside the low stone walls, to where the river swings west under a bare clay bank and the water lies deep and dark. If the bank flattens into reeds, you have gone past it. A crocodile lies in the pool under the cut. It suns on the bank at midday. It comes up at any traveller on it, day or night. Even badly hurt, it sinks into the pool and comes up again. The station's low wall stands above the cut. I suspect the landing's clay basket lies there, but I cannot swear to it. Go by day. Take care.", 38, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.two-charges.pay", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "Two drakes, received. Here is a dipper of the well's water. The stop is paid.", "Two drakes. Take the dipper.", "Two drakes, with thanks. Take the dipper. Rest safely within the walls.", 39, 4, 0, 3},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.two-charges.start", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "This season the stop is two drakes a head, up from one. The money is meant to pay a mason to re-line the well in stone. The crack on the ford side is new and a finger wide. The landing refused to haul stone. It does not build in stone and does not drink the well's water. Now the landing charges one drake a head to walkers who wade the ford. Any walker can wade it. I have never charged the landing for water. A mason's lining will hold. Pay me two drakes and I will give you a dipper of the well's water.", "Two drakes a head this season, up from one. It pays for a mason to re-line the cracked well in stone. The landing would not haul the stone. Pay, or go on.", "This season's account, plainly. The stop is two drakes a head, up from one. The well is Imperial-built. It is failing. A new crack runs a finger wide from the coping down the lining on the ford side. I raised the charge to pay a mason to re-line it in stone. I take no pleasure in the rise. The landing refused to haul stone. It does not build in stone and does not drink the well's water. Now the landing charges one drake a head to walkers who wade the ford. Any walker can wade it. I have never charged the landing for water. A mason's lining will hold. Pay me two drakes and I will give you a dipper of the well's water.", 40, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.well-keeper.two-charges.terms", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.well-keeper", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "My charge has not changed: two drakes a stop, to pay a mason. A proper lining will hold. If you will put terms to me, I am at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk. Signs-For-The-Cargo, the landing's poler, poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon. The raft is about 65 yards north of the well, across the ford.", "My charge stands: two drakes. If you will put terms to me, I am at the well in the morning and at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon. Signs-For-The-Cargo, the landing's poler, poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon.", "My charge has not changed, but I will hear honest terms. It is two drakes a stop, to pay a mason. A proper lining will hold. I am at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk. Signs-For-The-Cargo, the landing's poler, poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon. The raft and the landing stage are about 65 yards north of the well, across the ford. The round mud huts stand behind them on the far bank.", 41, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.about-blackwood", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.about-blackwood", "This is the Blackwood Road, traveller. West of the station it runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh. Then it goes on through the Blackwood hills to Leyawiin in Cyrodiil. East along it is Gideon. Ask me about Gideon.", "The Blackwood Road. West to Leyawiin, east to Gideon.", "This is the Blackwood Road, traveller. West of the station it runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh. Then it goes on through the Blackwood hills to Leyawiin in Cyrodiil. East along it is Gideon. Ask me about Gideon if you want to go that way.", -1, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.about-claywater", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.about-claywater", "Claywater is a mixed village where the road crosses the ford, traveller. An Imperial well and station house stand on one bank. Our Argonian landing stands on the other. The station folk count everything twice and drink from a cracked well.", "A village at a ford, traveller. The station is on that bank and the landing on this one.", "Claywater is a mixed village where the road crosses the ford. I am glad to tell you of it, traveller. An Imperial well and station house stand on one bank. Our Argonian landing stands on the other. The station folk count everything twice and drink from a cracked well. I would not drink it myself.", -1, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.about-gideon", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.about-gideon", "Gideon is the western frontier city, traveller, at the east end of the Blackwood Road, where the courts still work. From here it is about 640 yards east to the signpost at Cartwright's Cross. Then it is about 1,190 yards on to the city. That is a little over a mile in all.", "Gideon is east along the road. About 1,830 yards.", "Gideon is the western frontier city, traveller, at the east end of the Blackwood Road, where the courts still work. From here it is about 640 yards east to the signpost at Cartwright's Cross. Then it is about 1,190 yards on to the city. That is a little over a mile in all.", -1, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.about-imperial-legion-remnant", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.about-imperial-legion-remnant", "I cannot tell you why there are legionaries here, traveller. Gaius Vibius keeps a household in the village. Ask him.", "I cannot say. Ask Gaius Vibius.", "I cannot tell you why there are legionaries here. I will not guess. Gaius Vibius keeps a household in the village. Ask him.", -1, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.about-onkobra", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.about-onkobra", "I know the water at our ford by its taste, not its name, traveller. It is not the Onkobra. It runs west, away from Gideon. The Onkobra runs east through Gideon into the interior. Signs-For-The-Cargo poles our ford. Ask him.", "Not the Onkobra. That runs east through Gideon. Ask Signs-For-The-Cargo.", "I know the water at our ford by its taste, not its name, traveller. It is not the Onkobra. It runs west, away from Gideon. The Onkobra runs east through Gideon into the interior. Signs-For-The-Cargo poles our ford. He will tell you more.", -1, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.about-prison-road", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.about-prison-road", "This is not the Prison road, traveller. The Prison road is the old Imperial cordon road from Blackrose to Lilmoth, far to the south-east. The road through Claywater Station is the Blackwood Road.", "This is not the Prison road. This is the Blackwood Road.", "This is not the Prison road, traveller. Travellers often mistake it for ours. The Prison road is the old Imperial cordon road from Blackrose to Lilmoth, far to the south-east. The road through Claywater Station is the Blackwood Road.", -1, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.clay-bend.after-alive", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.lf83-clay-bend", "The crocodile still lies in the deep pool under the clay cut, traveller, where the landing digs its plaster clay. Keep off the cut. It comes up at anyone who stands there.", "The crocodile still lies in the pool under the cut. Keep off it.", "The crocodile still lies in the deep pool under the clay cut, traveller, where the landing digs its plaster clay. Keep off the cut. It comes up at anyone who stands there. I fear for whoever wades below it. Go by day, if you must go.", 42, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.clay-bend.after-dead", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.lf83-clay-bend", "The crocodile at the cut is dead, traveller. The landing can dig its clay there again, at the cut where the river swings west below the ford, on the station bank. No traveller is taken in that pool now.", "The crocodile at the cut is dead. The landing can dig its clay there again.", "The crocodile at the cut is dead, traveller. I am glad of it. The landing can dig its clay there again, at the cut where the river swings west below the ford, on the station bank. No traveller is taken in that pool now.", 43, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.clay-bend.stage-20", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.lf83-clay-bend", "Travellers slip along the station bank past the cut at night and wade the shallow tail below the pool, to dodge the landing's charge. The crocodile lies in that pool, traveller. We find their prints in the clay at dawn. The landing has dug its clay at that cut since before the well.", "Travellers wade the shallow tail below the cut at night, to dodge the landing's charge. The crocodile lies in that pool. The landing has dug its clay at that cut since before the well.", "I will tell you. Take care with it. Travellers slip along the station bank past the cut at night and wade the shallow tail below the pool, to dodge the landing's charge. The crocodile lies in that pool. We find their prints in the clay at dawn. I fear for them. The landing has dug its clay at that cut since before the well.", 44, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.clay-bend.stage-30", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.lf83-clay-bend", "Travellers slipped along the station bank past the cut at night and waded the shallow tail below the pool, to dodge the landing's charge. We found their prints in the clay at dawn. You have cleared that pool. I thank you. The landing has dug its clay at that cut since before the well.", "Travellers waded the shallow tail below the cut at night, to dodge the landing's charge. We found their prints in the clay. You have cleared that pool. The landing has dug its clay at that cut since before the well.", "I will tell you. I thank you for clearing the pool. Travellers slipped along the station bank past the cut at night and waded the shallow tail below the pool, to dodge the landing's charge. We found their prints in the clay at dawn. I feared for them. The landing has dug its clay at that cut since before the well.", 45, 4, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.claywater-station", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-station", "Claywater Station is two halves at one ford. They face each other over the water. The station has water, beds and a stable on its bank. We have the cart raft on ours. The round mud huts stand on the landing bank. Neither half can hold the other's bank.", "Two banks, one ford. Water and beds on that bank, the raft on this one.", "Claywater Station is two halves at one ford. They face each other over the water. The station has water, beds and a stable on its bank. We have the cart raft on ours. The round mud huts stand on the landing bank. Neither half can hold the other's bank. Ask me about the people or the work, if you want more.", -1, 4, 2, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.claywater-station-danger.after-30", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-station-danger", "I have no danger of my own to name, traveller. Signs-For-The-Cargo poles the raft and knows the ford better than I do. Ask him what he fears there.", "I have no danger to name. Ask Signs-For-The-Cargo.", "I have no danger of my own to name. I will not invent one for you. Signs-For-The-Cargo poles the raft and knows the ford better than I do. Ask him what he fears there.", 46, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.claywater-station-danger.before-30", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-station-danger", "A crocodile has taken the deep pool under our clay cut below the ford, traveller, where the landing digs its plaster clay. Keep away from the cut. Signs-For-The-Cargo, who poles the raft, will say more.", "A crocodile has taken the deep pool under our clay cut below the ford. Keep away from it.", "A crocodile has taken the deep pool under our clay cut below the ford, traveller, where the landing digs its plaster clay. Keep away from the cut. Do not go there alone and unready. Signs-For-The-Cargo, who poles the raft, will say more. So will I, if you ask me about the clay bend.", 47, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.claywater-station-danger.poler-dead", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-station-danger", "I have no danger of my own to name. I have no heart for it today. The landing mourns its poler.", "I have no danger to name. Leave me.", "I have no danger of my own to name. I have no heart for it today. The landing mourns its poler. Come back another day.", 48, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.claywater-station-directions", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-station-directions", "There are two ways, traveller. East along the Blackwood Road is Gideon: about 640 yards to the signpost at Cartwright's Cross, then about 1,190 yards on to the city. West the road runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh, then on through the Blackwood hills to Leyawiin in Cyrodiil.", "East is Gideon, about 1,830 yards. West is Leyawiin, past the marsh edge.", "There are two ways, traveller. I will give you both. East along the Blackwood Road is Gideon: about 640 yards to the signpost at Cartwright's Cross, then about 1,190 yards on to the city. West the road runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh, then on through the Blackwood hills to Leyawiin in Cyrodiil.", -1, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.claywater-station-people.base", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-station-people", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is the landing's poler. Livia Varinius is the well-keeper on the station bank. Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger keep the household hut with me, by the common on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning we cook at the common's fire. By day we work the common and the drying racks. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh are road travellers on the Blackwood Road. In the afternoon they sit on the bench by the brazier at the well. At night they pay for a bed in the station house.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo poles the raft. Livia Varinius keeps the well. Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger share my hut.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is the landing's poler. Livia Varinius is the well-keeper on the station bank. Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger keep the household hut with me, by the common on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning we cook at the common's fire. By day we work the common and the drying racks. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh are road travellers on the Blackwood Road. In the afternoon they sit on the bench by the brazier at the well. At night they pay for a bed in the station house. Ask Livia Varinius or Signs-For-The-Cargo. They will tell you their own side.", 49, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.claywater-station-people.keeper-dead", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-station-people", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is the landing's poler, traveller. Livia Varinius, the well-keeper, is dead. Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger keep the household hut with me, by the common on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning we cook at the common's fire. By day we work the common and the drying racks. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh are road travellers on the Blackwood Road. In the afternoon they sit on the bench by the brazier at the well. At night they pay for a bed in the station house.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo poles the raft. Livia Varinius is dead. Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger share my hut.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is the landing's poler, traveller. Livia Varinius, the well-keeper, is dead. I am sorry for it. Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger keep the household hut with me, by the common on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning we cook at the common's fire. By day we work the common and the drying racks. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh are road travellers on the Blackwood Road. In the afternoon they sit on the bench by the brazier at the well. At night they pay for a bed in the station house.", 50, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.claywater-station-people.poler-dead", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-station-people", "Signs-For-The-Cargo, the landing's poler, is dead, traveller. Livia Varinius is the well-keeper on the station bank. Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger keep the household hut with me, by the common on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning we cook at the common's fire. By day we work the common and the drying racks. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh are road travellers on the Blackwood Road. In the afternoon they sit on the bench by the brazier at the well. At night they pay for a bed in the station house.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is dead. Livia Varinius keeps the well. Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger share my hut.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo, the landing's poler, is dead, traveller. We mourn him. Livia Varinius is the well-keeper on the station bank. Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger keep the household hut with me, by the common on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning we cook at the common's fire. By day we work the common and the drying racks. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh are road travellers on the Blackwood Road. In the afternoon they sit on the bench by the brazier at the well. At night they pay for a bed in the station house.", 51, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.claywater-station-work", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-station-work", "The station has water, beds and a stable on its bank, traveller. Our work is the cart raft on this bank. Carts cross on it and pay by the wheel.", "The station has water, beds and a stable. We have the raft.", "The station has water, beds and a stable on its bank, traveller. Our work is the cart raft on this bank. Carts cross on it and pay by the wheel. Signs-For-The-Cargo poles it. He will tell you the rest.", -1, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.cracked-well.after-40", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.lf83-cracked-well", "Look at the well head, traveller. There is a band of fresh grey clay rammed in behind the coping and down the lining on the ford side. Clay holds where mortar cracks. It bends with the bank and keeps the ford out. The landing renews it each dry season.", "There is fresh grey clay behind the lining on the ford side. Clay holds where mortar cracks.", "Look at the well head, traveller. There is a band of fresh grey clay rammed in behind the coping and down the lining on the ford side. Clay holds where mortar cracks. It bends with the bank and keeps the ford out. The landing renews it each dry season. I will taste that water again when the clay has settled.", 52, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.cracked-well.after-other", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.lf83-cracked-well", "The lining is still cracked, traveller. Ford water and silt seep in through it, so the well water tastes of the ford. Mortar cracks with the moving bank. If clay is rammed behind the lining, it bends with the bank and keeps the ford out.", "The lining is still cracked. The ford seeps in. Mortar cracks. Clay would hold.", "The lining is still cracked, traveller. Ford water and silt seep in through it, so the well water tastes of the ford. I judge by taste, and I will not call that good water. Mortar cracks with the moving bank. If clay is rammed behind the lining, it bends with the bank and keeps the ford out. The landing renews it each dry season.", 53, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.cracked-well.ask", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.lf83-cracked-well", "I can tell you what is wrong with the station's water, traveller, because I judge everything by its taste. Bring me a dipper of it. Livia Varinius gives one to any traveller who has paid the stop. Do not take it unasked, because that is theft if she sees you. I will taste it against the ford water in the bucket by my door.", "I can tell you what ails the station's water. Bring me a dipper of it. Livia Varinius gives one to any traveller who has paid the stop. Do not take it unasked. I will taste it against the ford water in the bucket by my door.", "I can tell you what is wrong with the station's water, traveller. I am glad you asked me. I judge everything by its taste. Bring me a dipper of it from the well. Livia Varinius gives one to any traveller who has paid the stop. Do not take it unasked, because that is theft if she sees you. I will taste it against the ford water in the bucket by my door.", 54, 6, 0, 4},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.cracked-well.mending", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.lf83-cracked-well", "There is more, traveller. The well's lining has cracked every year. A woman of the landing draws her wash water at the well and has watched Livia Varinius mend it with a trowel each dry season. Livia keeps a jar of the morning bucket's water under the windlass cover at the well. She means it for a mason. She also writes each day's work at the well in the station ledger, which stays in the station house. Some travellers now wade the shallow tail of the river below the clay cut at night, to dodge the landing's charge.", "There is more. The well's lining has cracked every year. A woman of the landing has watched Livia Varinius mend it with a trowel each dry season. Livia keeps a jar of the morning bucket's water under the windlass cover. She writes each day's work at the well in the station ledger. Some travellers wade the shallow tail of the river below the clay cut at night, to dodge the landing's charge.", "There is more, traveller. You have earned it. The well's lining has cracked every year. A woman of the landing draws her wash water at the well and has watched Livia Varinius mend it with a trowel each dry season. Livia keeps a jar of the morning bucket's water under the windlass cover at the well. She means it for a mason. She also writes each day's work at the well in the station ledger, which stays in the station house. Some travellers now wade the shallow tail of the river below the clay cut at night, to dodge the landing's charge.", 55, 6, 0, 5},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.cracked-well.tasted", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.lf83-cracked-well", "Give it here. I will taste it against the ford water. Ah. That is the ford in it, traveller, with silt. The ford seeps into the well through the cracked lining, so the well water tastes of the ford. Mortar cracks when the bank moves. Clay behind the lining moves with it and keeps the ford out, until it is renewed each dry season. The landing set its charge on walkers only after the station raised its charge on the stop. I told Signs-For-The-Cargo that his charge is wrong, because travellers wade past the crocodile at night to avoid it. He would not hear it. Ask me again. I will tell you the rest.", "Give it here. I will taste it against the ford water. Ah. That is the ford in it, with silt. The ford seeps into the well through the cracked lining. Mortar cracks when the bank moves. Clay behind the lining moves with it and keeps the ford out, until the clay is renewed each dry season. The landing set its charge on walkers only after the station raised its charge on the stop. I told Signs-For-The-Cargo that his charge is wrong, because travellers wade past the crocodile at night to avoid it. He would not hear it. Ask me again. I will tell you the rest.", "Give it here. I will taste it against the ford water. Ah. That is the ford in it, traveller, with silt. The ford seeps into the well through the cracked lining, so the well water tastes of the ford. Mortar cracks when the bank moves. Clay behind the lining moves with it and keeps the ford out, until it is renewed each dry season. The landing set its charge on walkers only after the station raised its charge on the stop. I told Signs-For-The-Cargo that his charge is wrong, because travellers wade past the crocodile at night to avoid it. He would not hear it. You have done well to bring this. Ask me again. I will tell you the rest.", 56, 6, 0, 6},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.goodbye", "goodbye", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "Walk well, traveller. Mind the ford.", "Go on, then.", "Go well, traveller. May the water keep you. Come back to the landing when you have more to ask.", -1, 6, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.greeting.dry-start", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "Traveller. I judge every stranger by how their water tastes. I have not tasted yours yet. Everyone asks about the two charges at Claywater this season. Ask me, if you like.", "What do you want, traveller? Everyone complains of the two charges this season, so I expect you will too.", "Welcome, traveller. Well met. I judge everyone by how their water tastes. I say yours is good water. You will want to hear about the two charges at Claywater. Everyone does this season.", 57, 6, 1, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.greeting.stage-10", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "Traveller. Have you heard Livia Varinius at the well and Signs-For-The-Cargo at the raft? I can say the two charges again if you need them.", "You again, traveller. Have you heard the keepers yet?", "Welcome back, traveller. Have you heard Livia Varinius at the well and Signs-For-The-Cargo at the raft? I will say the two charges again, as often as you need.", 58, 7, 1, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.greeting.stage-20", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "Traveller. If you want to know what ails the station's water, I can tell you, because I judge everything by its taste. Ask me about the failing well.", "Traveller. If it is the well you want to ask about, ask. I tell little to strangers.", "Welcome back, traveller. If you want to know what ails the station's water, I will tell you gladly. I judge everything by its taste. I have tasted that well. Ask me about the failing well.", 59, 8, 2, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.greeting.stage-40", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "You brought both banks to one charge, traveller. We have rammed clay behind the cracked lining before the rains. Travellers need not wade below the cut at night now.", "One charge now, traveller. The clay goes in before the rains.", "Welcome, traveller. Well met. You brought both banks to one charge. I thank you. We have rammed clay behind the cracked lining before the rains. Travellers need not wade below the cut at night now.", 60, 10, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.greeting.stage-41", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "You paid Signs-For-The-Cargo so that walkers pay once, at the well. That is done, traveller. The well is still cracked.", "Walkers pay once now, traveller. The well is still cracked.", "Welcome, traveller. You paid Signs-For-The-Cargo so that walkers pay once, at the well. I know why you did it. The well is still cracked. I will say so to any traveller who asks.", 61, 10, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.greeting.stage-42", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "Livia Varinius has dropped her charge back to the old drake. Signs-For-The-Cargo has dropped the walkers' charge in answer. No mason will come. The well is still cracked.", "Both charges came down, traveller. The well is still cracked.", "Welcome, traveller. Livia Varinius has dropped her charge back to the old drake. Signs-For-The-Cargo has dropped the walkers' charge in answer. No mason will come. The well is still cracked.", 62, 10, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.greeting.stage-90", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "The rains came before you made terms, traveller. The well is still cracked. Travellers still pay at both banks or wade below the ford at night.", "The rains came, traveller. Nothing was settled.", "Traveller, you are welcome, though I have bad news to give. The rains came before you made terms. The well is still cracked. Travellers still pay at both banks or wade below the ford at night.", 63, 10, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.greeting.stage-92", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "Livia Varinius is dead, traveller. The well has no keeper now. The station's charge ended with her. The landing keeps its charge on the ford.", "Livia Varinius is dead, traveller. Leave it be.", "Traveller, you are welcome, but I am sorry to say this. Livia Varinius is dead. The well has no keeper now. The station's charge ended with her. The landing keeps its charge on the ford.", 64, 10, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.greeting.stage-93", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is dead, traveller. The raft has no poler now. The landing will make no terms with the station while it mourns. Both charges stand.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo is dead, traveller. Leave it be.", "Traveller, you are welcome, but I am sorry to say this. Signs-For-The-Cargo is dead. The raft has no poler now. The landing will make no terms with the station while it mourns. Both charges stand.", 65, 10, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.greeting.start", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "", "Traveller. I judge every stranger by how their water tastes. I have not tasted yours yet. What do you want to know?", "What do you want, traveller?", "Welcome, traveller. Well met. I judge everyone by how their water tastes. I say yours is good water. Ask me what you like.", 66, 10, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.role-two-halves", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.role-two-halves", "The station has water, beds and a stable on one bank. We have the cart raft on the other. Carts cross on the raft and pay by the wheel.", "The station has water and beds. We have the raft.", "The station has water, beds and a stable on one bank. We have the cart raft on the other. Carts cross on the raft and pay by the wheel.", -1, 10, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.two-charges.stage-0", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "Both banks charge you more this season for one stop, traveller. Livia Varinius, the well-keeper, raised the station's charge from one drake to two, to pay a mason to re-line the well in stone. Signs-For-The-Cargo, the landing's poler, now takes one drake a head from walkers who wade the ford. Before, only carts on the raft paid. A crocodile has taken the deep pool under our clay cut below the ford. The rains are close, so we must replaster our walls before them. Hear Livia at the well and Signs at the raft. Judge them yourself.", "Both banks charge you more this season. Livia Varinius at the well took her charge from one drake to two. Signs-For-The-Cargo at the raft takes a drake from every walker at the ford. There is a crocodile at our clay cut and the rains are close. Ask them, if you must.", "Sit with me a moment. I will say it plainly. Both banks charge you more this season for one stop. Livia Varinius, the well-keeper, raised the station's charge from one drake to two, to pay a mason to re-line the well in stone. Signs-For-The-Cargo, the landing's poler, now takes one drake a head from walkers who wade the ford. Before, only carts on the raft paid. A crocodile has taken the deep pool under our clay cut below the ford, where we dig our plaster clay. The rains are close. We must replaster our walls before them. Hear Livia at the well and Signs at the raft. Judge them yourself.", 67, 10, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.two-charges.stage-10", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "Livia Varinius charges two drakes for the stop and Signs-For-The-Cargo charges one drake a head to wade, traveller. You will find Livia at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk. Signs poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon. A crocodile has taken the deep pool under our clay cut. The rains are close, so we must replaster our walls soon.", "Livia Varinius is at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk. Signs-For-The-Cargo poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon. The rains are close. Go.", "I will say it again, traveller, as often as you need. Livia Varinius charges two drakes for the stop and Signs-For-The-Cargo charges one drake a head to wade. You will find Livia at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk. Signs poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon. A crocodile has taken the deep pool under our clay cut. The rains are close. We must replaster our walls before them.", 68, 10, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.two-charges.stage-20", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "The clay cut is below the ford on the station bank, traveller. From the well, go about 45 yards west, outside the low stone walls, to where the river swings west under a bare clay bank and the water lies deep and dark. If the bank flattens into reeds, you have gone past it. Our clay basket lies at the cut, where the crocodile came up. It comes up at whoever stands on the cut, so go by day, or look down on it from the station's low wall above the cut. The rains are close. We must replaster our walls before them.", "The cut is about 45 yards west of the well, outside the low stone walls, where the river swings west under a bare clay bank. Our basket lies there. The crocodile comes up at whoever stands on the cut. The rains are close.", "The clay cut is below the ford on the station bank. I will tell you the way. From the well, go about 45 yards west, outside the low stone walls, to where the river swings west under a bare clay bank and the water lies deep and dark. If the bank flattens into reeds, you have gone past it. Our clay basket lies at the cut, where the crocodile came up. It comes up at whoever stands on the cut, so go by day, or look down on it from the station's low wall above the cut. The rains are close. We must replaster our walls before them. Come back and tell me when it is done.", 69, 10, 2, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.two-charges.stage-30", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "You have the basket back, traveller. The rains are close. We must replaster our walls before them. Livia Varinius charges two drakes for the stop and Signs-For-The-Cargo charges one drake a head to wade, so put your terms to both. Livia is at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk. Signs poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon.", "You have the basket back. The rains are close. Livia Varinius is at the well in the morning and Signs-For-The-Cargo is at the raft. Put your terms to them.", "You have the basket back. I thank you. The rains are close. We must replaster our walls before them. Livia Varinius charges two drakes for the stop and Signs-For-The-Cargo charges one drake a head to wade, so put your terms to both. Livia is at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk. Signs poles the raft in the morning and is at the drying racks behind it in the afternoon.", 70, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.two-charges.stage-40", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "There is one charge now, traveller. The stop costs two drakes, one drake to each bank. It is the fair charge that I wanted. The landing rammed its clay in behind the cracked lining before the rains. Livia Varinius sends for no mason.", "One charge now. The stop costs two drakes, one to each bank. The clay is rammed in. That is fair.", "There is one charge now, traveller. I thank you for it. The stop costs two drakes, one drake to each bank. It is the fair charge that I wanted. The landing rammed its clay in behind the cracked lining before the rains. Livia Varinius sends for no mason. No traveller was taken at the cut for it.", 71, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.two-charges.stage-41", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "You paid Signs-For-The-Cargo 100 drakes to take no charge from walkers this season, traveller. Now travellers pay once, two drakes at the well. The well is still cracked. I wanted a fair charge. This one was bought.", "You paid Signs-For-The-Cargo a hundred drakes. That bought the poler. It is not a fair charge.", "You paid Signs-For-The-Cargo 100 drakes to take no charge from walkers this season, traveller. Now travellers pay once, two drakes at the well. The well is still cracked. I know you meant well by it. But I wanted a fair charge. This one was bought. Signs-For-The-Cargo has been quieted.", 72, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.two-charges.stage-42", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "Livia Varinius dropped her charge back to the old drake, traveller. She did it so that the yearly mending would not be talked of. The landing dropped its walkers' charge in answer. The well is still cracked. The charges are fair again.", "Both charges came down. The well is still cracked. The charges are fair again.", "Livia Varinius dropped her charge back to the old drake, traveller. She did it so that the yearly mending would not be talked of. The landing dropped its walkers' charge in answer. The well is still cracked. The charges are fair again. I am glad of that. No traveller has cause now to wade the dark water to save a drake. I thank you for it.", 73, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.two-charges.stage-90", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "The rains came to Claywater Station before any terms were made, traveller. Both charges stand. The well is still cracked.", "The rains came and no terms were made. Both charges stand. The well is still cracked.", "The rains came to Claywater Station before any terms were made, traveller. Both charges stand. The well is still cracked. I am sorry for it.", 74, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.two-charges.stage-92", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "Livia Varinius died before terms were made, traveller. The windlass at the well stands idle. The landing keeps its charge at the ford. Now the well has no keeper with whom terms can be made.", "Livia Varinius died before terms were made. The windlass stands idle. The landing keeps its charge.", "Livia Varinius died before terms were made, traveller. I am sorry for it. The windlass at the well stands idle. The landing keeps its charge at the ford. Now the well has no keeper with whom terms can be made.", 75, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.n1-3.two-charges.stage-93", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n1-3", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "Signs-For-The-Cargo died before terms were made, traveller. The raft is tied up at the landing stage. Both charges stand. He was one of ours. I am sorry for it.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo died before terms were made. The raft is tied up. Both charges stand.", "Signs-For-The-Cargo died before terms were made, traveller. The raft is tied up at the landing stage. Both charges stand. He was one of ours. I am sorry for it.", 76, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.about-blackwood", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.about-blackwood", "The Blackwood Road crosses the Claywater ford here. East, about 640 yards from the station, is a signpost at Cartwright's Cross. Gideon lies about 1,190 yards on, a little over a mile in all. West of the station the road runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh, then on through the Blackwood hills to Leyawiin in Cyrodiil.", "East to Gideon, a little over a mile. West to Leyawiin, past the edge of the marsh.", "The Blackwood Road crosses the Claywater ford here, traveller. East, about 640 yards from the station, is a signpost at Cartwright's Cross. Gideon lies about 1,190 yards on, a little over a mile in all. West of the station the road runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh, then on through the Blackwood hills to Leyawiin in Cyrodiil.", -1, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.about-claywater", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.about-claywater", "Claywater Station is a mixed village where the road crosses the Claywater ford. An Imperial well and station house stand on one bank. Our landing stands on the other. The landing is older than the station. Two languages are spoken here, one from each bank.", "A village where the road crosses the ford. Two banks.", "Claywater Station is a mixed village where the road crosses the Claywater ford. An Imperial well and station house stand on one bank. Our landing stands on the other. The landing is older than the station. Argonian polers worked the ford before the Imperials dug the well. Two languages are spoken here, one from each bank.", -1, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.about-gideon", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.about-gideon", "Gideon is the western frontier city, at the east end of the Blackwood Road. From the station it is about 640 yards east to the signpost at Cartwright's Cross, then about 1,190 yards on to the city, a little over a mile in all. Gideon has the last working courthouse. Disputes are settled there on signed paper. Here a quarrel goes to me on our bank and to the well-keeper on the other.", "Gideon is east along the Blackwood Road, a little over a mile.", "Gideon is the western frontier city, at the east end of the Blackwood Road. From the station it is about 640 yards east to the signpost at Cartwright's Cross, then about 1,190 yards on to the city, a little over a mile in all. Gideon has the last working courthouse. Disputes are settled there on signed paper. Here a quarrel goes to me on our bank and to the well-keeper on the other. If you have a quarrel with a neighbour here, bring it to me or to Livia Varinius.", -1, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.about-helstrom", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.about-helstrom", "Helstrom lies far east of Gideon, traveller. It is the interior capital. It has grown into a Hist grove. Canoes reach it from Gideon down the Onkobra white water. I pole a ford and cannot tell you of white water.", "Helstrom lies far east of Gideon. Canoes reach it down the Onkobra white water.", "Helstrom lies far east of Gideon, friend. It is the interior capital. It has grown into a Hist grove. Canoes reach it from Gideon down the Onkobra white water. I pole a ford and cannot tell you of white water. I will gladly tell you of the ford and the road instead.", -1, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.about-onkobra", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.about-onkobra", "That is not the Onkobra, traveller. The Onkobra runs east through Gideon into the interior. The stream at my ford runs west, away from Gideon. It is shallow and stony here, so a walker can wade it and a cart cannot.", "That is not the Onkobra. The Onkobra runs east through Gideon. My stream runs west.", "That is not the Onkobra, traveller, though many ask. The Onkobra runs east through Gideon into the interior. The stream at my ford runs west, away from Gideon. It is shallow and stony here, so a walker can wade it and a cart cannot. That is why carts need my raft.", -1, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.about-prison-road", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.about-prison-road", "The Prison road is the old Imperial cordon road from Blackrose to Lilmoth, far to the south-east, traveller. It is not this road. The road through Claywater Station is the Blackwood Road.", "The Prison road is far to the south-east. This is the Blackwood Road.", "The Prison road is the old Imperial cordon road from Blackrose to Lilmoth, far to the south-east, friend. It is not this road. The road through Claywater Station is the Blackwood Road. It crosses my ford.", -1, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.clay-bend.after-alive", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-clay-bend", "A crocodile still lives in the deep pool under the clay cut, traveller, where the landing digs its plaster clay. Stay off the cut.", "A crocodile still lives in the pool under the cut. Stay off it.", "A crocodile still lives in the deep pool under the clay cut, friend, where the landing digs its plaster clay. It comes up at whoever stands on the cut. Keep to the ford and the road.", 77, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.clay-bend.after-dead", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-clay-bend", "The crocodile at the cut is dead, traveller. The landing can dig its clay there again.", "The crocodile is dead. The landing can dig at the cut again.", "The crocodile at the cut is dead, friend. The landing can dig its clay there again. You have our thanks for it.", 78, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.clay-bend.alive", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-clay-bend", "The landing digs its plaster clay at the cut below the ford, on the station bank, as we did before the well. From the well, go about 45 yards west, outside the low stone walls, to where the river swings west under a bare clay bank and the water lies deep and dark. If the bank flattens into reeds, you have gone past it. A crocodile has the deep pool under the cut and comes up at whoever stands on it. The landing has not dug for ten days. Our basket lies there. How it came to lie there is not for strangers. The rains are close. The landing will hear terms from whoever gives it back its cut before them. Ask Takes-The-Short-Weight, who tastes everything, what ails the station's water. She lives in the round mud hut on our bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning she sits at the landing's fire, about 50 yards north of the raft.", "The landing digs its plaster clay at the cut below the ford, on the station bank, about 45 yards west of the well. A crocodile has the deep pool under it. Our basket lies there. How it came to lie there is my business. Takes-The-Short-Weight tastes everything. Ask her what ails the station's water. She is in the round mud hut on the landing bank, about 30 yards north of the raft.", "The landing digs its plaster clay at the cut below the ford, on the station bank, as we did before the well. From the well, go about 45 yards west, outside the low stone walls, to where the river swings west under a bare clay bank and the water lies deep and dark. If the bank flattens into reeds, you have gone past it. A crocodile has the deep pool under the cut and comes up at whoever stands on it, day or night. The landing has not dug for ten days. Our basket lies there. The rains are close. The landing will hear terms from whoever gives it back its cut before them. How the basket came to lie there I will tell you when the crocodile is dead. Ask Takes-The-Short-Weight, who tastes everything, what ails the station's water. She lives in the round mud hut on our bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning she sits at the landing's fire, about 50 yards north of the raft.", 79, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.clay-bend.dead", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-clay-bend", "The crocodile is dead, so I will say what I kept back. I dropped the landing's clay basket at the cut when it came up at me. I ran. I am ashamed of it.", "It is dead, so I say it. I dropped the landing's basket at the cut when the crocodile came up at me. I ran.", "The crocodile is dead, friend, so I will say what I kept back. I dropped the landing's clay basket at the cut when it came up at me. I ran. I am ashamed of it. I tell you because you have earned it.", 80, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.claywater-station", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-station", "Claywater Station is two halves at one ford. The station has its well and its house on one bank. The landing has the raft and the huts on the other. Neither half can hold the other's bank. The landing is older. We are proud of the ford.", "Two halves at one ford. Neither holds the other's bank.", "Claywater Station is two halves at one ford, traveller. The station has its well and its house on one bank. The landing has the raft and the huts on the other. Neither half can hold the other's bank. Argonian polers worked the ford before the Imperials dug the well. We are proud of it.", -1, 12, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.claywater-station-danger", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-station-danger", "A crocodile has taken the deep pool under the clay cut below the ford, where the landing digs its plaster clay. It comes up at whoever stands on the cut. Stay off it.", "A crocodile has the pool under our clay cut. Stay off the cut.", "A crocodile has taken the deep pool under the clay cut below the ford, where the landing digs its plaster clay. It comes up at whoever stands on the cut, so keep to the ford and the road. Ask about the clay bend if you mean to go there.", 81, 12, 1, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.claywater-station-danger.after", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-station-danger", "The crocodile that held the pool under the cut is dead. I know of no other danger here.", "The crocodile at the cut is dead. I have no other danger to name.", "The crocodile that held the pool under the cut is dead, friend. I know of no other danger here.", 82, 13, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.claywater-station-directions", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-station-directions", "Go east along the Blackwood Road for Gideon: about 640 yards to the signpost at Cartwright's Cross, then about 1,190 yards on to the city, a little over a mile in all. For Leyawiin, go west: the road runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh, then on through the Blackwood hills. The signpost's arms point east to Gideon and back west to Leyawiin. The Drowning Gate is on the way east, a painted pole barrier in a field off the road.", "East for Gideon, a little over a mile. West for Leyawiin.", "Go east along the Blackwood Road for Gideon: about 640 yards to the signpost at Cartwright's Cross, then about 1,190 yards on to the city, a little over a mile in all. For Leyawiin, go west: the road runs about 450 yards to the edge of Black Marsh, then on through the Blackwood hills. The signpost's arms point east to Gideon and back west to Leyawiin. The Drowning Gate is on the way east, a painted pole barrier in a field off the road. At the station, the well stands at the station house door. The raft and the landing stage are about 65 yards north of the well, across the ford. The round mud huts are behind them on our bank.", -1, 13, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.claywater-station-people", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-station-people", "Livia Varinius is the well-keeper. She is at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk. Takes-The-Short-Weight, Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger keep the household hut by the common on our bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning they cook at the common's fire. By day they work the common and the drying racks. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh are road travellers on the Blackwood Road. In the afternoon they sit on the bench by the brazier at the well. At night they pay for a bed in the station house.", "Livia Varinius keeps the well. Takes-The-Short-Weight, Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger are on our bank. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh sit at the well in the afternoon.", "Livia Varinius is the well-keeper. She is at the well in the morning, at the counter by the station house door in the afternoon and at the stable at dusk. Takes-The-Short-Weight, Gaius Vibius and Keeps-The-Second-Ledger keep the household hut by the common on our bank, about 30 yards north of the raft. In the morning they cook at the common's fire. By day they work the common and the drying racks. Abhuki and Mee-Seesh are road travellers on the Blackwood Road. In the afternoon they sit on the bench by the brazier at the well. At night they pay for a bed in the station house. You will find them all easily, friend.", -1, 13, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.claywater-station-work", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-station-work", "The station has water, beds and a stable on its bank. The landing has the cart raft. A plank ferry carries carts across the ford. I pole it in the morning. In the afternoon I am at the drying racks behind it, where our fish dry.", "The station has water, beds and a stable. I have the raft.", "The station has water, beds and a stable on its bank. The landing has the cart raft. A plank ferry carries carts across the ford. I pole it in the morning. In the afternoon I am at the drying racks behind it, where our fish dry. A cart pays by the wheel. I count every load that way.", -1, 13, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.ford-charge.after-41", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-ford-charge", "I took your hundred drakes, traveller. The landing takes no charge from walkers this season. Walkers wade the ford free and pay once, at the well. Carts still pay by the wheel.", "I took your hundred drakes. Walkers wade free this season.", "I took your hundred drakes, friend. I keep my word. The landing takes no charge from walkers this season. Walkers wade the ford free and pay once, at the well. Carts still pay by the wheel.", 83, 13, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.ford-charge.after-other", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-ford-charge", "The hundred drakes for the walkers' season were never paid, traveller. That price is closed. Ask me about the two charges at Claywater. I will tell you how the banks stand.", "That price is closed. Ask me about the two charges.", "The hundred drakes for the walkers' season were never paid, friend. That price is closed. Ask me about the two charges at Claywater. I will tell you how the banks stand.", 84, 13, 1, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.ford-charge.bought", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-ford-charge", "A hundred drakes. The landing takes no charge from walkers this season. It is paid. Walkers wade the ford free. Carts still pay by the wheel on the raft.", "A hundred drakes. Taken. No walker pays the landing this season.", "A hundred drakes. The landing takes no charge from walkers this season. It is paid, friend. I keep my word. Walkers wade the ford free. Carts still pay by the wheel on the raft.", 85, 14, 0, 7},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.ford-charge.price", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-ford-charge", "Walkers pay one drake a head to wade the ford this season. Carts pay by the wheel. For a hundred drakes I take no charge from walkers this season. You do not carry a hundred drakes now. Come back when you do.", "A hundred drakes. You do not carry that. Come back when you do.", "Walkers pay one drake a head to wade the ford this season. Carts pay by the wheel. For a hundred drakes I take no charge from walkers this season. You do not carry a hundred drakes now, friend. Come back when you do. We will settle it.", 86, 14, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.goodbye", "goodbye", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "", "Stay moist, traveller.", "Go on, then.", "Stay moist, friend. Come back across when you like.", -1, 14, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.greeting", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "", "Welcome, traveller. I pole the raft in the morning. In the afternoon I am at the drying racks behind it. A cart pays by the wheel.", "State your business, traveller. The raft is here.", "Welcome, friend. I pole the raft in the morning. In the afternoon you will find me at the drying racks behind it. Tell me what you need. I count every load by its wheels.", -1, 14, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.greeting.after-40", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "", "You brought both banks to one charge, traveller. It is two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. The landing has rammed its clay behind the lining.", "You settled the stop, traveller. It is one charge now.", "Welcome, friend of the landing. You gave us back our cut and you settled the stop. It is two drakes a stop now, one drake to each bank. Our clay is rammed behind the lining. We owe you.", 87, 14, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.greeting.after-41", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "", "Walkers wade the ford free this season, traveller, because you paid the hundred drakes. They pay once, at the well. The well is still cracked.", "You paid, so walkers wade free this season. That was the bargain.", "Welcome, traveller. With your hundred drakes I took no charge from walkers this season. I keep my bargains. They pay once, at the well. The well is still cracked.", 88, 14, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.greeting.after-42", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "", "Livia Varinius has put her charge back to the old drake. The landing has dropped the walkers' charge in answer. Walkers wade the ford free now. You did that, traveller.", "Livia Varinius has dropped her charge. I have dropped the walkers' charge. Cross.", "Welcome, friend. Livia Varinius has put her charge back to the old drake. The landing has dropped the walkers' charge in answer. Walkers wade the ford free now. You did that.", 89, 14, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.greeting.after-90", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "", "The rains have come, traveller. No terms were made. Both charges stand.", "The rains have come. Both charges stand.", "The rains have come, friend. No terms were made. Both charges stand. I wish I could say otherwise.", 90, 14, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.greeting.after-92", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "", "Livia Varinius is dead, traveller. The station's charge ended with her. The landing's charge stands on the ford. I have little heart to talk of it.", "Livia Varinius is dead. I have nothing to say.", "Livia Varinius is dead, friend. The station's charge ended with her. The landing's charge stands on the ford. I have little heart to talk of it. Stay a while if you wish.", 91, 14, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.greeting.dry-start", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "", "Welcome to the landing, traveller. Walkers pay one drake a head to wade the ford this season. Carts pay by the wheel on the raft. If the two charges at Claywater puzzle you, ask me.", "One drake a head to wade, traveller. Carts pay by the wheel. Ask me about the two charges at Claywater if you must.", "Welcome, traveller. Well met. Walkers pay one drake a head to wade the ford this season. Carts pay by the wheel on the raft. The two charges at Claywater are the talk of the road. Ask me about them. I will answer plainly.", 92, 14, 1, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.landing-terms", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-landing-terms", "No stone, ever. Mortar cracks with the moving bank and lets the ford in. Clay rammed behind a wall bends with the bank and keeps the ford out. We renew it each dry season, when we renew our walls. One charge would be two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. The landing's drake would pay for the clay. But there is no clay until the basket is back from the cut. The rains are close. I set the walkers' charge when the station raised its own. Takes-The-Short-Weight told me the walkers' charge is wrong, because travellers wade past the crocodile at night to avoid it. I would not hear it.", "No stone, ever. We ram clay behind any wall on this bank. It bends with the bank and keeps the ford out. One charge of two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank, would do it. The landing's drake would pay for the clay. There is no clay until the basket is back from the cut. The rains are close. Why I set the walkers' charge, I do not tell strangers.", "Listen, friend, because this is the landing's whole offer. No stone, ever. Mortar cracks with the moving bank and lets the ford in. Clay rammed behind a wall bends with the bank and keeps the ford out. We renew it each dry season, when we renew our walls. One charge would be two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. The landing's drake would pay for the clay. But there is no clay until the basket is back from the cut. The rains are close. I will say the rest, since you ask. I set the walkers' charge when the station raised its own. Takes-The-Short-Weight told me the walkers' charge is wrong, because travellers wade past the crocodile at night to avoid it. I would not hear it. I wish I had.", 93, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.landing-terms.after-40", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-landing-terms", "I said no stone, ever. I said clay rammed behind the lining. Livia Varinius heard it through you, traveller. The clay is rammed in behind the cracked lining. The one charge covers the clay: two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. We renew it each dry season.", "I said no stone. I said clay behind the lining. Livia Varinius heard it. The clay is rammed in.", "I said no stone, ever. I said clay rammed behind the lining. Livia Varinius heard it through you, friend. The clay is rammed in behind the cracked lining. The one charge covers the clay: two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. It bends with the bank. We renew it each dry season.", 94, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.landing-terms.after-other", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-landing-terms", "I offered clay rammed behind the lining, traveller. I never offered stone. It bends with the bank and keeps the ford out. The offer was one charge of two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. It was never made a bargain.", "I offered clay behind the lining. I offered no stone. It was never made a bargain.", "I offered clay rammed behind the lining, friend. I never offered stone. It bends with the bank and keeps the ford out. The offer was one charge of two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. It was never made a bargain. I wish it had been.", 95, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.one-charge.after-40", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "The landing agreed, traveller. It is one charge, two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. Livia Varinius sends for no mason, because the landing rammed its clay in behind the lining before the rains.", "The landing agreed. Our clay is rammed in. It is one charge.", "The landing agreed gladly, friend. It is one charge, two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. Livia Varinius sends for no mason, because the landing rammed its clay in behind the lining before the rains.", 96, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.one-charge.after-other", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "The one charge was never agreed, traveller. The landing would have bought its clay behind the lining with its one drake of the two a stop.", "The one charge was never agreed. I would have taken two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank.", "The one charge was never agreed, friend. The landing would have bought its clay behind the lining with its one drake of the two a stop. I would have kept to it.", 97, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.one-charge.agrees", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "You have the basket. You have shown me this is a crack that clay seals, not a new lining. Then the landing agrees. I take the basket. The landing will ram clay behind the well's lining and renew it each dry season, before the rains close. The one charge is two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. Our drake pays for the clay.", "You have the basket. You have shown me a crack that clay seals. Then the landing agrees. I take the basket. We will ram clay behind the lining before the rains.", "You have the basket, friend. You have shown me this is a crack that clay seals, not a new lining. Then the landing agrees, gladly. I take the basket. The landing will ram clay behind the well's lining and renew it each dry season, before the rains close. The one charge is two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. Our drake pays for the clay.", 98, 15, 0, 8},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.one-charge.argued", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "You say the well has a crack that clay seals, not a lining to re-lay. I have no answer to that. Mortar cracks with the moving bank. Clay bends with it. If the well needs only a crack sealed, there is no stone to haul. I give up the objection. Ask me again about one charge. I will take the basket.", "You say the well has a crack that clay seals, not a lining to re-lay. I have no answer to that. I give up the stone objection. Ask me again about one charge. I will take the basket.", "You argue it fairly, friend. You say the well has a crack that clay seals, not a lining to re-lay. I have no answer to that. I would not hide it if I had. Mortar cracks with the moving bank. Clay bends with it. If the well needs only a crack sealed, there is no stone to haul. I give up the objection. Ask me again about one charge. I will take the basket.", 99, 15, 0, 9},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.one-charge.no-clay", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "There is no clay to give, traveller. The landing's basket is still at the cut. Bring it back. Then we will talk of one charge before the rains.", "There is no clay to give. The basket is not with you. Bring it back from the cut. Then we will talk of one charge.", "I would give it gladly, friend, but there is no clay to give without the basket. Bring it back from the cut. Then we will talk of one charge before the rains.", 100, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.one-charge.no-seal", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.lf83-one-charge", "The station only wants stone. The landing will not haul it. Mortar cracks with the moving bank. Clay does not. Show me this is a crack that clay seals. Look at the well. Ask Takes-The-Short-Weight, who tastes everything. I do not give the landing's clay on a stranger's word.", "The station wants stone. The landing will not haul it. Show me the crack is one that clay seals. Look at the well. Ask Takes-The-Short-Weight, who tastes everything. She is in the round mud hut on our bank, about 30 yards north of the raft.", "The station only wants stone. The landing will not haul it. Mortar cracks with the moving bank. Clay does not. Show me this is a crack that clay seals, friend. Then I will give it. Look at the well. Ask Takes-The-Short-Weight, who tastes everything. I trust you, but the landing's clay is not mine alone to give.", 101, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.role-poling", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.role-poling", "A cart crosses the ford on my plank raft. Carts pay by the wheel. Walkers can wade the ford, which is shallow and stony. This season they pay one drake a head to do it. I pole in the morning and work the racks in the afternoon.", "A cart crosses on my plank raft. Carts pay by the wheel.", "A cart crosses the ford on my plank raft. I am proud of it. Carts pay by the wheel. I count every load by its wheels. Walkers can wade the ford, which is shallow and stony. This season they pay one drake a head to do it. I pole in the morning and work the racks in the afternoon.", -1, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.two-charges.after-40", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "The banks keep one charge now, traveller: two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. Our clay is rammed in behind the cracked lining. The lining is not being rebuilt. The ferry at the Drowning Gate, the painted pole barrier in the field off the road, carries you free for settling it.", "One charge now: two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. The ferry at the Drowning Gate, the painted pole barrier in the field off the road, carries you free.", "The banks keep one charge now, friend. You made it. It is two drakes a stop, one drake to each bank. Our clay is rammed in behind the cracked lining. The lining is not being rebuilt. We owe you. The ferry at the Drowning Gate, the painted pole barrier in the field off the road, carries you free for settling it.", 102, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.two-charges.after-41", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "You paid me a hundred drakes, traveller. The landing takes no charge from walkers this season. They pay two drakes once, at the well. The well is still cracked.", "You paid the hundred drakes. Walkers wade free this season. They pay once, at the well.", "You paid me a hundred drakes, friend. I keep my bargains. The landing takes no charge from walkers this season, so they pay two drakes once, at the well. The well is still cracked.", 103, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.two-charges.after-42", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "Livia Varinius put her charge back to the old drake, so that her yearly mending would not be talked of. The landing dropped the walkers' charge in answer. Walkers wade free now. The well is still cracked. The ferry at the Drowning Gate, the painted pole barrier in the field off the road, carries you free.", "Livia Varinius put her charge back to the old drake. The landing dropped the walkers' charge. Cross free.", "Livia Varinius put her charge back to the old drake, friend, so that her yearly mending would not be talked of. The landing dropped the walkers' charge in answer. Walkers wade free now. The well is still cracked. The ferry at the Drowning Gate, the painted pole barrier in the field off the road, carries you free.", 104, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.two-charges.after-90", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "The rains came before any terms were made, traveller. Both charges stand: the station's at the well, the landing's at the ford. The well is still cracked.", "The rains came. No terms were made. Both charges stand.", "The rains came before any terms were made, friend. Both charges stand: the station's at the well, the landing's at the ford. The well is still cracked.", 105, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.two-charges.after-92", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "Livia Varinius died before terms were made, traveller. The windlass stands idle. The landing keeps its charge at the ford.", "Livia Varinius died before terms were made. The windlass is idle. The landing keeps its charge.", "Livia Varinius died before terms were made, friend. The windlass stands idle. The landing keeps its charge at the ford.", 106, 15, 0, -1},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.two-charges.pay", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "One drake, received. You may wade the ford, traveller. The landing has its due.", "One drake. Taken. Wade the ford.", "One drake, with thanks, friend. Wade the ford. Mind the stones. The landing has its due.", 107, 15, 0, 10},
    {"line.claywater-station.landing-s-poler.two-charges.tell", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.landing-s-poler", "topic.claywater-two-charges", "This season the landing charges one drake a head to wade the ford. Before, only carts on the raft paid. They pay by the wheel still. Argonian polers worked this ford before the Imperials dug their well. The landing refused to haul stone for the Imperials' new lining. We do not build in stone. We do not drink the well's water. The rains are close. Our walls need plaster. A crocodile has settled in the deep pool at our clay cut. Ask me about the ford charge if you want the walkers to go free. I keep the reason for the charge for those whom I trust. If you mean to wade, the charge is one drake. Ask me again with a drake in hand. Then you may wade.", "One drake a head to wade this season. Carts pay by the wheel on the raft. The Imperials want a new lining for their well. The landing will not haul stone for it. The rains are close. A crocodile has settled in the deep pool at our clay cut. I keep the reason for the charge to myself until I know you. If you mean to wade, it is one drake. Ask me again with a drake in hand.", "Sit a moment, traveller. I will tell it plainly. This season the landing charges one drake a head to wade the ford. Before, only carts on the raft paid. They pay by the wheel still. Argonian polers worked this ford before the Imperials dug their well. The landing refused to haul stone for the Imperials' new lining. We do not build in stone. We do not drink the well's water. The rains are close. The landing must replaster its walls before them. A crocodile has settled in the deep pool at our clay cut. If you want the walkers to go free, ask about the ford charge. I will keep back the reason for the charge a while longer. If you mean to wade, the charge is one drake. Ask me again with a drake in hand. Then you may wade.", 108, 15, 2, -1},
    {"greeting.claywater-station-n2.base", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "", "What does walker want of Abhuki?", "Walker talks too much. This one is busy.", "Ah, walker. Come, ask this one.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"greeting.claywater-station-n2.crime", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "", "Walker should not have done that. Abhuki has heard.", "Abhuki saw it. Walker had best go.", "Abhuki saw, walker. Do not do it again.", 109, 17, 0, -1},
    {"greeting.claywater-station-n2.high", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "", "Sit, walker. The brazier has room.", "Walker may stand.", "Sit, friend. The warm side is yours.", 110, 17, 0, -1},
    {"greeting.claywater-station-n2.night", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "", "Awake too, walker? The coals are still warm.", "Walker should be asleep. This one is.", "Come sit, walker. The brazier has coals yet.", 111, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.about-blackwood", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.about-blackwood", "It goes up. Blackwood is the hill country in the west. The Blackwood Road climbs up through those hills to Cyrodiil. A pack feels every step of a climb.", "The Blackwood Road climbs through the hills to Cyrodiil. Go and see.", "West and up, friend. The Blackwood Road climbs through the Blackwood hills to Cyrodiil. Take a good cloak for the climb.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.about-claywater", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.about-claywater", "One ford, two banks, two halves of a village. The half with the well and the station house is timber frame and masonry. The well is cracking in its stone. This one has heard the Argonians will not help mend it. The brazier is the best part.", "The station half is timber frame and masonry. The well is cracking.", "Claywater is a ford with two halves, friend. Mine, the station half, is timber frame and stone. Sit by the brazier and watch the well.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.about-gideon", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.about-gideon", "Walkers on this road talk of Gideon all day. The courts there still work. An Owing is a debt worked off in labour. When one is made in Gideon it is written on paper, so the bound one can take it to the court and contest it. This one has the pack to carry and no Owing to carry with it.", "Gideon has courts and they still work. An Owing made there is a paper that a court can contest.", "Gideon's courts still work, friend. An Owing is a debt worked off in labour. If one is made in Gideon it is a paper contract, so the bound one can contest it in court.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.about-imperial", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.about-imperial", "Black Marsh had its coasts and border lands held by the Empire. It never held the deep marsh. What it built was roads, road stages and prisons. Then it withdrew from the province. This one sits at one of its stages today, by a brazier at a well it dug.", "The Empire held coasts and borders, not the deep marsh. It built roads, stages and prisons. Then it withdrew.", "The Empire held the borders and coasts of Black Marsh, friend, but not the deep marsh. It built roads, road stages and prisons. Then it withdrew. The stages still serve a traveller.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.about-onkobra", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.about-onkobra", "The Onkobra flows past Gideon, heading east into the heart of the province. The road that follows its bank is muddy. A pack sits better on a dry back than a wet one, so this one waits for dry days.", "The Onkobra runs east. The road beside it is muddy.", "Mind the mud on the Onkobra road, friend. The river runs east from Gideon. The road beside it is muddy. Wait for a dry day.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.about-prison-road", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.about-prison-road", "The Prison road is the one with the Tag House beside it, up on a dry rise above the mud. This one would pick that rise over the road itself on any wet night. Where the road ends, Abhuki cannot say. She knows only what stands beside it.", "The Tag House stands by the Prison road, on a dry rise. That is all this one knows of it.", "Look for the Tag House, friend. It stands beside the Prison road on a dry rise. A good place to be out of the mud.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.claywater-station", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.claywater-station", "Where does this one sit, you ask? By the brazier at the well, with her pack close against her leg. A station is a stop on the road, not a home. The station house is on this bank. Across the ford, the landing huts sit low by the channel. Those Argonians poled the crossing long before anyone dug the well.", "A stop on the road. The well is on this bank, the landing across the ford. Ask the well-keeper for the rest.", "Sit down by the brazier, friend. This one will show you the place with her hand. The station house is here on the near bank. The landing huts across the ford are older than the well.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.claywater-station-danger", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.claywater-station-danger", "Bog dogs, you ask? They prowl both banks at dawn and again at dusk, so this one keeps to her brazier at those hours. A crocodile lives in the channel and keeps to it. It is no trouble if you stay out of the water. The dogs are different. A hungry dog will go round a camp half the night, sniffing at every bundle on the ground.", "Bog dogs on the banks at dawn and at dusk. A crocodile in the channel. Keep away from both.", "Stay by the brazier at dawn and dusk, friend. Bog dogs prowl the banks then. The crocodile keeps to the channel, so keep out of the water. A dog finds a pack by its smell, this one has heard.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.claywater-station-directions", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.claywater-station-directions", "The road east is easy to find. Take the track to the Blackwood Road, then follow the road east. Cartwright's Cross is a few minutes off it. Next comes Mile House of the Eagle, after some fifteen minutes along the road. Gideon is about twenty-five minutes on from the turning. This one would reach the Mile House before dark.", "East by the track, then the Blackwood Road. Cartwright's Cross, the Mile House, Gideon, in that order.", "It's easy, friend. East on the track to the Blackwood Road, then keep going. Cartwright's Cross comes first, Mile House of the Eagle after it, Gideon last. Rest at the Mile House if the light goes.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.claywater-station-people", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.claywater-station-people", "The station bank is where the Imperial families live. The Argonian families are across the ford on the landing bank. Imperials bring a quarrel to the well-keeper. Argonians bring theirs to the poler. This one finds Argonians fair in trade. They weigh honestly. They remember every coin you owe them.", "Imperials on this bank, Argonians on that one. Imperials bring a quarrel to the well-keeper. Argonians bring theirs to the poler. This one keeps out of both.", "Imperial families are on the station bank. Argonian families are on the landing bank. The well-keeper hears the Imperial quarrels. The poler hears the Argonian ones. Trade with the Argonians, friend. They weigh honestly.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.claywater-station-work", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.claywater-station-work", "A plain arrangement pleases this one. On the station bank, you find water, a counter, beds upstairs and a stable. The landing across the water keeps the crossing. A traveller pays twice for one stop. The station bank charges for its half. The landing charges for the other half. Neighbours on both banks dislike travellers who wade over to dodge a charge.", "Water, beds and a stable on this bank. The crossing on that one. The station charges for the beds. The landing charges for the crossing. It's coin twice. This one pays it.", "The station bank has water, beds and a stable. The landing has the crossing. Each side charges you for its part, so carry coin for both, friend. Wading over to dodge one charge only annoys the neighbours.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2.role-road", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2", "topic.role-road", "The Blackwood Road is what this is. The Empire built it. Carts still roll on it between Leyawiin and Gideon. On the way, a traveller passes Cartwright's Cross and Mile House of the Eagle. In the monsoon season, the road closes. This one would not like to be caught on the wrong side of that with a pack to keep dry.", "The Blackwood Road, an Imperial road. Carts run it between Leyawiin and Gideon. Cartwright's Cross and Mile House of the Eagle lie along it. It closes in the monsoon season.", "The Blackwood Road is Imperial work. Carts run along it between Leyawiin and Gideon. You pass Cartwright's Cross and Mile House of the Eagle. Plan around the monsoon season, friend, because the road closes then.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"greeting.claywater-station-n2-2.base", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "", "You come from the Gideon road, sir?", "Not from Gideon, then. Go your way.", "Sir, you came at the right time. What news of Gideon?", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"greeting.claywater-station-n2-2.crime", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "", "That was a crime, sir.", "I watched you do it. Do it far from my sight.", "That was a crime, sir. Put it right before Gideon.", 112, 17, 0, -1},
    {"greeting.claywater-station-n2-2.high", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "", "Good, sir. I hoped you would pass again.", "Back already. I hoped for a better face.", "Sir, you are back. Sit and tell me of the road.", 113, 17, 0, -1},
    {"greeting.claywater-station-n2-2.night", "greeting", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "", "Any word of the Gideon road tonight?", "Ask me of the road in daylight.", "Sit down, sir. What is said of Gideon tonight?", 114, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.about-blackwood", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.about-blackwood", "West of here, the hill country is called Blackwood. The road I mean to take goes up through those hills into Cyrodiil. The hill folk stay close to the roots of their own tree and ask strangers few questions. A riddle will still get a word out of them.", "", "", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.about-claywater", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.about-claywater", "Two halves share this ford. The station bank is timber and stone. The landing bank is mud and thatch. A traveller pays the station for its half of the stop and the landing for the other. I pay twice for one night.", "", "", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.about-gideon", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.about-gideon", "Gideon is the frontier city out west. Its courts still sit. That matters to a man like me. An Owing is a debt you work off with your hands. One made in Gideon is a paper contract, so a court will hear you contest it. I want a paper with my name on it.", "Gideon is a frontier city with working courts.", "Gideon is the frontier city out west, with courts that still sit. I will tell you what I know of the paper there. Tell me what you know of the road.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.about-onkobra", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.about-onkobra", "The Onkobra starts near Topal Bay. From there it flows east, passing Gideon, then on into the province's heart. The track along its bank is muddy and in poor repair. Red clay from its banks sells well in the marsh. I'd walk that track only in the dry.", "", "", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.about-prison-road", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.about-prison-road", "This road ends at Gideon. That is the road I follow. The Prison road and the Border road were laid by the Empire. The Mile House was an Imperial waystation. I have not walked any of the three.", "Old Imperial roads. Not mine.", "The Prison road and the Border road are old Imperial work, while the Mile House was a waystation. I have not walked them, but I am glad to say so.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.about-sul-xan", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.about-sul-xan", "The Sul-Xan are Naga who take souls. They put on jade death masks and sacrifice ojel and Argonians both. Every tribe fears them. Traders here mention a mask found at a border post. I want to be in Gideon behind a court door before I hear more.", "", "", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.claywater-station", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.claywater-station", "I'm only a traveller here. I pay for a bed at the station house. The well and the counter are on this bank. The landing across the ford is older than all of it, since the polers worked this crossing before the Imperials dug a stone. You came by the Gideon road? Then you have walked further than I have.", "Ask the well-keeper. I only pay for a bed.", "Sit by me at the well. I will tell you what I have learnt of this ford. You can tell me of the road.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.claywater-station-danger", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.claywater-station-danger", "Bog dogs run the banks at dawn and again at dusk, so I stay inside at both hours. A crocodile lies in the channel. Wait for full light before you set off, because the road to Gideon is long enough without a bite in it.", "Dogs at dawn and dusk. A crocodile in the channel. Stay indoors.", "Bog dogs and a crocodile are the whole of it. I walk the ford at midday. You should do the same.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.claywater-station-directions", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.claywater-station-directions", "Take the track east from the ford, a few minutes, to the Blackwood Road. You have walked it before? Cartwright's Cross is a short walk off it to the north-west. Some fifteen minutes east along the road, a track turns toward Mile House of the Eagle. Gideon is some twenty-five minutes along the road, then a few turnings.", "East from the ford to the Blackwood Road. Gideon is at its far end.", "East from the ford, a few minutes, to the Blackwood Road. Cartwright's Cross is off it, then Mile House of the Eagle. Gideon is some twenty-five minutes along the road, then a few turnings. I will draw it in the dust if you wish.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.claywater-station-people", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.claywater-station-people", "Imperial families live by the well. The Argonians live in the huts across the ford. When two neighbours fall out, the Imperials go to the well-keeper and the Argonians go to the poler. I'm a customer to both banks. You learn quickly which of them wants paying first.", "Two banks, two sets of neighbours. Pay both.", "Imperial or Argonian, they will serve you if you pay first. I can tell you who to pay first.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.claywater-station-work", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.claywater-station-work", "I don't work here, I just pay. I sleep at the station house, then walk down to the landing in the morning. The poler poles carts across the ford on a raft of planks, since a cart can't wade the stones. I'm saving my coin for the courts at Gideon.", "Work is for those who stay. I pay and I leave.", "You will want a seat on the raft. Pay the poler before the planks are loaded.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
    {"override.claywater-station-n2-2.role-road", "dialogue", "npc.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.n2-2", "topic.role-road", "It's the Blackwood Road, an Imperial road. Carts use it between Leyawiin and Gideon. You pass Cartwright's Cross on the way, then Mile House of the Eagle. The road closes in the monsoon season, so I mean to reach Gideon before the rains.", "It's the Blackwood Road. It closes in the monsoon season.", "It's the Blackwood Road, which carts use between Leyawiin and Gideon. The monsoon shuts it, so start before the rains.", -1, 17, 0, -1},
}};
